  speakerName: Irah
  speakerPortrait: {fileID: 0}
  dialogueText: 'When someone gives you a helping hand, you can thank them specifically
    for their assistance.

    In Ilokano, ''agyamanak iti tulong mo'' means ''thank
    you for your help.''

    You can use it when someone helps you complete a task
    or solve a problem.

    Now, try saying ''agyamanak iti tulong mo'' yourself.'
